    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0079" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v07/pg40"/>

                <head>20. National Security Decision Memorandum 77<anchor n="1" xml:id="d20-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-08-12">August 12, 1970</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="to">
                    <head>TO</head>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                    <item>The Director of Central Intelligence</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Air Activity in Southeast Asia Over FY 71</item>
                </list>
                <p>Following the VSSG review,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d20-f2"/> the President has directed that the Department of Defense
                    shall: <pb facs="0080" n="41" xml:id="pg41"/>
                    <list>
                        <item>—Provide funding adequate to support an FY 1971 air activity level of
                            14,000 tactical air (USAF, USN and USMC), 1,000 B–52, and 1,000
                            gunship sorties monthly in Southeast Asia.</item>
                        <item>—Authorize a lower sorties level than funded—between 10,000 and 14,000
                            tactical air sorties flown monthly in Southeast Asia—depending upon
                            circumstances as determined by COMUSMACV.</item>
                        <item>—Plan to compensate for this reduction in U.S. air activity by
                            continuing DOD’s intensive effort to
                            enhance the capabilities of the VNAF to at least 4,300 sorties monthly
                            and of the RLAF to 2,000 sorties
                            monthly during FY 71.</item>
                        <item>—Plan to close two bases in South Vietnam (Chu Lai and Tuy Hoa) during
                            FY 1971 and to place one base in Thailand (Takhli) on a caretaker basis
                            until a further review.</item>
                        <closer>
                            <signed>
                                
                                    <hi rendition="#bold">Henry A. Kissinger</hi>
                                
                            </signed>
                        </closer>
                    </list>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
